    "turn_text": "Well, Caleb, I appreciate the clarification because the United States can't end the civil war. I mean, we can support Martin Griffiths in trying to bring it to an end, but we can at least eliminate our involvement and take constructive steps to reduce the extraordinary suffering. The president took a constructive step in stopping our support of the offensive Saudi bombing in Yemen. But the blockade continues and the blockade is U.S. back. We need to make it very clear that the Saudis need to stop the blockade that's causing starvation of children. I mean, they're not allowing food in there and not allowing medicine. The second thing we have to do is make sure that the Saudis are not funding or frankly that Iran is not funding. internal parties in Yemen, make it a civil war, don't have the Saudis, UAE or Iran funding the parties. Because until that funding rise up, the war will continue. So those are two things that I have called on President Biden to do.",
