    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66007.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, and the question for the Pentagon is what is going to be effective policy? If you want to safeguard our troops. If you care about the safety of troops, the biggest way to safeguard those troops is to start bringing them home. You can't have them sitting in Iraq, taking on going of fire from Iranian militias. And then we're in this awful situation where we get hit and we feel understandably compelled to respond. perpetuate the cycle of violence putting our troops at risk. Now they did a tremendous job, our troops, in defeating ISIS, which had to be done in my view. We couldn't allow ISIS to have territorial control and become a caliphate. But that job was done in 2018. Why are we still there? And what is the plan of getting us out?",
