  {
    "episode_id": 66007,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66007.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "I think he should follow the timeline now if we're talking about a month or two months or three months that he has a view of, okay, we want to do it by the end of August to do it properly. And if he and that there's some flexibility, I don't think he has to follow it to the letter of what Trump said out. But if we're come fall, still talking about being in Afghanistan, I think he's going to have a bipartisan criticism from Congress, which once our troops out, Most of the people in Congress are they going to groups out? So yes, I think at that point, if there's no alternative, I mean, if he says, well, I have a different approach, I want to withdraw and give me tell the fall, I think people will be illicit. But if it's indefinite, then yes, he will be responsible.",
