    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Topic Shift"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 66007,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66007.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "You know, honestly, Matt Gates, I know every time I mentioned him positively, I get about 100 tweets negatively on my account. But he's been very strong. And Yemen, he was strong on not getting into war. in Iran, in not building up an even greater troop presence overseas. Rand Paul has been strong. There are people in the Freedom Caucus. Andy Briggs, we disagree with a lot, but Andy Briggs has been strong on issues of North Korea, trying to resolve that situation. So this is not an issue with just of the progressive left. There is a sense of this country. that were overextended, that that was never our founding intent. I mean, I know there's all this talk about the British monarchy these days, and I get maybe being of Indian origin, I take it personally, you know, given the British Empire. But, you know, America was never an empire. That's our fundamental greatness, that unlike Britain, we never had this desire to colonize the world. We never had this desire to project force all over the world. So why we are in these endless wars, it's concrete to who we are as a people.",
