  {
    "episode_id": 66007,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66007.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "You voted for impeachment of the now former president on January 13th when he was still in office for his behavior leading up to an on January 6th. The Senate was 10 votes shy of conviction. I believe that Republicans broadly don't have much of an appetite for understanding, much less vocalizing of exactly what happened on that day. What does that mean for them, do you think?",
