  {
    "episode_id": 66007,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66007.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 29,
    "turn_text": "Because I saw how the Patriot Act was abused after 9-11 and how ordinary Americans were subject to surveillance, were subject to profiling. And just like I wouldn't want a Pakistani American subject to being profiled if they were good citizens, I wouldn't want a a Trump supporter who is abiding the subject to profiling or surveillance because of who they are. I think that we have plenty of tools available to go after those who actually commit these crimes. One of the things I would say to law enforcement is just getting a bunch of young people to follow parlor Instagram, Facebook more, and you probably won't need all these other tools. You just need some people, folks, who are a little bit more tech savvy, and you could probably craft a lot of what you need.",
